From: Prakharrdev <prakhar06.work@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:05:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Claim a WhatsApp connection by Meta app and prove every
 Graph call

Meta sets the webhook address per app, not per phone number, so two
connections on one app (even for different numbers) would fight over
the same callback. The connection now carries the app's App ID and is
claimed by it. Saving checks the token was issued for that app, asked
with the app's own id and secret, which also proves the secret.

Every Graph API call now carries appsecret_proof, not only the check
made when the connection is saved, so an app with Require App Secret
turned on accepts sends, media and read receipts too. The media
download itself goes to Meta's media host rather than Graph and takes
no proof.
